Falsifies `entropy_contract::verification::readiness_is_reported_exactly_when_a_first_byte_is_nonzero`.

The defect: `readiness` looks at the first byte of the draw only, the check that reads "the first
word is zero" one byte wide. A working device whose draw opens with a zero byte is then reported
dead.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!` on `READY`, with a draw whose first byte is zero
and a later one is not.

diff --git a/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -164,7 +164,7 @@ pub const fn bring_up_failure(step: u64) -> u64 {
 /// `first`.
 pub fn readiness(first_bytes: impl IntoIterator<Item = u8>) -> u64 {
     let mut seen = false;
-    for byte in first_bytes {
+    for byte in first_bytes.into_iter().take(1) {
         if byte != 0 {
             return READY;
         }
